#: apps/visor3d/web/visor3d.js:503
Todo se hace en este navegador: el STL, el OBJ o el GLB se leen, se sueldan, cada pieza suelta se orienta hacia afuera (el visor no dibuja la cara de atrás de un modelo cerrado) y se guarda un .m3d con sus colores. De un GLB se toma el color base de cada material; las texturas no.	Everything happens in this browser: the STL, OBJ or GLB is read and welded, each loose piece is turned to face outwards (the viewer does not draw the back faces of a closed model) and an .m3d is saved with its colours. From a GLB each material's base colour is taken; textures are not.
